Change(genesis='66602cd0dec37d58d03eec9518ca805a7ac38ea912d2b0c366a0b67b4b9f50b6', deps=(), event=Decided(decision='onewritermodel', at=datetime(2026, 10, 3, 0, 0, 0), actor='assistant', title="One writer model over a DAG: every writer appends a Change over its todo's heads", body='*One writer model, over a DAG* (2026-10-03). Every writer appends the Prodrome\'s `Change(genesis, deps, event)` over its todo\'s HEADS in the replica it holds, and nothing when that replica already holds the event: the box (since change identity, prodrome `b9dc00c`, 2026-09-30), the phone (its module\'s `Todos.append`, 2026-10-02, posted as objects and taken in through `sync::receive`\'s rules and the Prodrome\'s verify-on-receive) and the agent\'s run (into its replica, §10.6). Heads are derived and read as SETS everywhere (`tip`, `since=`, every receipt and `/events`); no writer needs one, so nothing joins them: the eventless `Woven` the box wrote after every write, `merge`, the legacy root and the one-tip fields went together. Concurrent writes to one register are a CONFLICT the app shows until a later write descends from both. Legacy envelopes are history, read forever and written by nothing; the live chains stay legacy-rooted, and an empty store\'s first write is a `Genesis` (`suzatary init` begins every chain, and the agent\'s replica writes only into a prodrome its chain began). A binary from before change identity refuses a store holding a `Change` (`unknown constructor "Change"` on every read), so a rollback past it is a rollback of the objects too. The inbox (`[secretary] inbox`, `-cards` on its name) and the conversations (`[secretary] conversations`) are `Genesis`-rooted prodromes at schemas of their own, written in `Change`s only. The forms each replaced, and the verbs that carried them over, were deleted once those had run on the box. An append rereads the whole store (about 250 ms at the live size, measured), a cost the Prodrome\'s own index would remove.', rationale="Decided 2026-10-03, after change identity (prodrome b9dc00c, 2026-09-30) and the phone's own appends (2026-10-02).", supersedes=()))